# AvaKit project rules

This is an Avalanche dapp built with AvaKit (`@avakit/react` + `@avakit/core`).

## UI

- Use **shadcn/ui only**. `@avakit/react` ships shadcn-styled components — match that style.
- **Black & white only** for now. Dark/light is wired via `next-themes`; every screen must work in both. Add brand colors later by editing the tokens in `app/globals.css`.
- Animations: **Framer Motion** or **GSAP** only.

## Wallet & chain

- Wallet button: `<ConnectAvalanche />`.
- Read state with hooks: `useAvaAccount`, `useAvaChain`, `useBalance`, `useContract`.
- For raw transactions, get a viem wallet client: `getWalletClient(chain, provider)` where `provider` comes from `useAvaKit()`.
- This app runs on `__CHAIN_CONST__` from `@avakit/core/chains` (`fuji` = Fuji testnet, `cChain` = C-Chain mainnet), set in `app/providers.tsx`. Fuji is the default; mainnet is an explicit choice, and every transaction there spends real AVAX.
- `app/providers.tsx` derives the wallets from the chain. Testnet: a temporary burner wallet, social login and injected wallets. Mainnet: no burner wallet, and social login only with your own client ID. Keep that split when you edit it.

## Safety

- Never hardcode RPC URLs or secrets. Use the chain config and `.env.local`.
- Private keys live in the wallet provider, never in app code.
- Social login needs no setup on a testnet: on localhost it works through a bundled demo Web3Auth key. Set your own `NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3AUTH_CLIENT_ID` (free, dashboard.web3auth.io, Sapphire Devnet) before deploying — the demo key only allows localhost. On mainnet there is no demo fallback: social login stays disabled until you set your own Sapphire Mainnet client ID.
